skipped_dates.description:
Dates of the rule on which the local start time does not exist (`nonexistent_local_time`, a spring-forward
gap) or exists twice (`ambiguous_local_time`, an autumn repeated hour): no class is scheduled on them;
schedule one as a one-time class with an explicit offset if wanted. Detail views only.

status.description:
`unavailable`: the gym is a draft (no first run until setup completes). `not_started`: offer it.
`in_progress`: started on some client and not ended; offer to resume. `completed` / `dismissed`: final;
never offer it again (replaying the tour is client-only and records nothing).

SessionTokens.description:
Credentials of a SimpleFit session. Send `access_token` as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` until
`access_token_expires_at`, then refresh. `refresh_token` is present only for the body transport;
with the cookie transport it is in the `Set-Cookie` header and never readable by scripts.

SponsorApplicationSaveRequest.description:
Any subset of the answers; only those change, each validated now (an invalid save changes nothing). `null`
clears an answer. Starting an application needs at least one non-blank answer and `client_request_id`;
every later save needs `expected_revision`.
